h fashion trends to offer the best pieces to customers and is enjoying running her business.\n  - effort: Gina is putting forth new offers and promotions in her online store to attract new customers as she works to grow her business.\n  - Gina: Gina built a new website for customer orders and encouraged Jon about his dance studio challenges. She was referenced by Jon and identified as Shia Labeouf.\n  - my journey: Gina mentioned that her journey is inspiring others.\n  - brand identity: Gina is working on building relationships and creating a strong brand image for her store, acknowledging Jon's advice that these are key.\n  - new offers and promotions: Gina is using new offers and promotions in her online store, which customers love, to drive sales and grow her customer base while starting her business.\n  - Gina: Gina owns a clothing store, built a new website, encouraged Jon about his dance studio, and told Jon to \"Just do it!\" after joking about Shia LaBeouf.\n  - sales: Gina is focused on growing her customer base, seeing more sales due to new offers and promotions on her online store, and looking for unique, trendy pieces.\n  - relationships: Gina is always working on building relationships and creating a strong brand image for her store.\n  - Gina: Gina advises Jon on marketing, is growing her online store, and asked Jon when he is opening his dance studio. She expressed excitement for his studio opening.\n  - Rome: Gina mentioned that Rome wasn't built in a day while encouraging Jon about finding investors for his dance studio.\n  - cool content: Gina suggested creating cool content and managing Jon's social media accounts.\n  - wholesalers: Gina emailed wholesalers for her clothing store, and one replied affirmatively, allowing her to expand and get closer to customers.\n  - Gina: Gina is an assistant who conversed with Jon about his new dance studio business, encouraging him after he lost his job.\n  - business project: Jon plans to build a focused busi