NTITIES>\n  - who I really am: Caroline found out who she really is with invaluable help from friends, family, and mentors during tough times, and now wants to pass that support to others.\n  - trans people: Caroline attended a special, empowering transgender poetry reading where trans people shared stories to celebrate identities. Caroline plans counseling for trans people focusing on self-acceptance support.\n  - trans woman: Caroline shared a painting representing her path as a trans woman; colors symbolize smashing rigid thinking about the binary gender system and loving her authentic self.\n  - transition: Caroline found creating art important during her transition to understand and accept herself, specifically while exploring her gender identity.\n  - gender identity: Caroline mentioned that creating art, like painting and drawing, was important during her transition to understand and accept her gender identity.\n  - Embracing Identity: 'Embracing Identity' is a topic about finding comfort and love in being yourself. Caroline's aim for the related painting was to show warmth, love, and self-acceptance, featuring a woman representing the journey of acceptance.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - transgender teen: Caroline mentors a transgender teen like herself, focusing on building confidence and finding positive strategies. They attended an LGBT pride event last month.\n  - Caroline: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday. She is excited to build a family by adopting needy kids, viewing adoption as a way to give back, show love, and acceptance.\n  - Oscar: Oscar is Caroline's guinea pig,