gies. They attended an LGBT pride event last month.\n  - the trans community: Caroline spoke about her transgender journey at a school event to encourage involvement in the LGBTQ community and give a voice to the trans community.\n  - journey: Caroline discussed her transgender journey, which started three years ago and involved volunteering at an LGBTQ+ youth center to support young people. Melanie praised her progress and authenticity.\n  - transgender stories: Caroline found the transgender stories from the LGBTQ support group she attended yesterday to be inspiring and felt thankful for the support.\n  - transgender community: Melanie asked Caroline what motivated her decision to transition and join the transgender community.\n  - transgender journey: Caroline created a plate for a local church reflecting her transgender journey and acceptance of growth and change, expanding on her previous discussion about her transition at a school event.\n  - hope: Caroline learned from an LGBTQ conference that tough times don't last, as hope and love exist.\n  - support and encouragement: Caroline appreciated Melanie's support and encouragement regarding her talk on her transgender journey, which aimed to inspire others and promote inclusivity.\n  - trans experience: Caroline uses her art to express her trans experience, showing her story and helping others understand the trans community.\n  - trans folks: Caroline uses her art to tell stories and teach people about trans folks, according to Melanie.\n  - growth and change: Caroline made a plate for a local church illustrating time changing lives, which represents her journey as a transgender woman and the importance of accepting growth and change.\n  - LGBTQ+ pride parade: Caroline mentioned attending an LGBTQ+ pride parade a few weeks ago to Melanie, who reacted positively to a picture Caroline shared.\n  - transition: Caroline found creating art important during her transition to understand and accept herself, specifically