ories: Joanna believes meaningful stories come from personal experiences and feelings, and she writes best when being true to herself, even if difficult.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be the best thing ever, a mix of highs and lows. Writing is an escape, a way to express feelings, and healing.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her feelings, act as an escape, put thoughts down, and create something good from them, as words have a magical way of healing.\n  - Rejections: Joanna received rejections from a film contest, which Nate acknowledged as tough but encouraged her to keep trying.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience as a mix of highs and lows, and that her journal is her rock, viewing writing as a huge part of her life.\n  - love story: Joanna is writing a movie script for a love story that involves many challenges; she is working hard and hopes to see it on the big screen.\n  - hard work: Joanna found seeing her hard work in writing a movie script acted out on the big screen a surreal and satisfying experience, the third time this has happened.\n  - journey: Joanna values the journey, appreciating happy moments to stay focused on dreams, and looks forward to showing it to Nate.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - writer: Joanna, identified as a writer, experienced a major setback when her laptop crashed, resulting in the loss of all her work.\n  - inspiring quotes: Joanna's cork board is filled with inspiring quotes and pictures for motivation and creativity.\n  - creatures: Joanna noted that the creatures bring much calm and joy