ing the camaraderie and hard work with his team. He recently ate a frog treat and enjoyed the win.\n  - John: John recently returned from an awesome trip to Italy, finding inspiration in its food, history, and architecture, and bought a cookbook there. He also admires Aragorn's bravery and justice.\n  - John: John enjoyed an awesome trip to Italy last month. He recently secured an endorsement with a popular beverage company, which he finds rewarding.\n  - John: John started doing seminars helping people with sports and marketing. He bought top-notch hiking and outdoor gear and had a successful photoshoot in a forest.\n  - John: John found a new gym and is training to stay fit for his professional basketball game, adapting his routine for balance. He also discussed film memories with Tim.\n  - John: John got an endorsement with a popular beverage company last week. Previously, John acknowledged Tim's study abroad plans for Galway, Ireland, next month.\n  - John: John got an endorsement deal with a popular beverage company last week. He previously started doing seminars on sports and marketing for aspiring professors.\n  - John: John congratulated Tim on getting into a study abroad program in Galway, Ireland. John also reported success in a game event that raised money for charity.\n  - John: John scored 40 points last week, his highest ever, contributing to a tough win with an electric atmosphere. He celebrated this incredible experience with his teammates.\n  - John: John and his wife went on an amazing road trip along the European coastline, enjoying spectacular views and bonding.\n  - John: John got an endorsement with a popular beverage company last week. He previously found yoga awesome, noting improvements in strength, flexibility, focus, and balance, and enjoys new world adventures.\n  - John: John congratulated Tim and mentioned achieving a career-high in assists during a game against a rival last Friday.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1917,"context_chars":7761,"retrieval_duration":0.2643287181854248,"response_duration":3.4918744564056396,"total_duration":3.7562031745910645,"grade":false,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer states that John did not get an ankle injury in 2023, which contradicts the gold answer that specifies an injury around November 16, 2023.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides specific information about John's ankle injury occurring on November 16, 2023, which directly answers the question. The relevant facts indicate that John was experiencing difficulties related to his injury on that date, confirming the timing of the injury. Therefore, all necessary details to answer the question are present in the context.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["John hurt his ankle during last season.","John has been experiencing difficulties related to an injury during the current week. (event_time: 2023-11-16T15:59:00Z)","The doctor stated that the injury is not serious (event_time: 2023-11-16T15:59:00Z)","Tim hopes John's injury heals soon. (event_time: 2023-11-16T15:59:00Z)"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_7","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_7_qa_46","category":"2","difficulty":"unknown","query":"How long did Jolene work on the robotics project given to her by her Professor?","golden_answer":"four months","hypothesis":"Jolene began working on the robotics project assigned by her engineering professor on February 1, 2023. She finished her engineering project last month, which was recorded on May 6, 2023. Therefore, she worked on the robotics project from February 1, 2023, until May 6, 2023.\n\nTo calculate the duration:\n- From February 1 to May 6 is 3 months and 5 days.\n\nThus, Jolene worked on the robotics project for approximately 3 months and 5 days.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Jolene is busy with a large robotics project assigned by her engineering professor (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene is working on a tough but fun robotics project that requires creativity and problem-solving (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene finished the engineering project last month. (event_time: 2023-05-06T00:00:00Z)\n  - Jolene's engineering professor gave her a large robotics project (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene has been working on a big project lately. (event_time: 2023-04-09T16:30:00Z)\n  - Jolene is currently enjoying working on the robotics project (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - The robotics project requires Jolene to solve puzzles related to design and programming (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene put in significant effort on the engineering project. (event_time: 2023-05-06T00:00:00Z)\n  - Jolene is currently working on a prototype. (event_time: 2023-08-12T20:50:00Z)\n  - The robotics project is testing Jolene's creative skills. (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene found a solution to a problem within her engineering project. (event_time: 2023-03-24T00:00:00Z)\n  - Jolene finished an electrical engineering project (event_time: 2023-01-16T00:00:00Z)\n  - Jolene finally finished the tough engineering project (event_time: 2023-05-06T00:00:00Z)\n  - Jolene achieved significant accomplishments with her engineering project (event_time: 2023-02-09T21:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene felt a mix of excitement and nervousness when receiving the robotics project (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Jolene had a big breakthrough with the project. (event_time: 2023-06-26T09:17:00Z)\n  - Jolene finds seeing the robot come together to be awesome (event_time: 2023-02-01T19:03:00Z)\n  - Deborah is asking Jolene how finishing the engineering project has inspired Jolene to keep striving for her dreams. (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:56:00Z)\n  - Jolene wants to continue working in engineering. (event_time: 2023-02-04T09:48:00Z)\n  - Jolene is balancing engineering school (event_time: 2023-02-25T16:50:00Z)\n  - Jolene considers finishing the engineering project ('it') a big milestone. (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:56:00Z)\n  - Jolene is most interested in getting involved in certain projects. (event_time: 2023-08-26T17:33:00Z)\n  - Research is key to Jolene's success (event_time: 2023-08-26T17:33:00Z)\n  - What Jolene learned in school is being applied to real projects (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:56:00Z)\n  - Jolene utilized her engineering skills. (event_time: 2023-02-04T09:48:00Z)\n  - Jolene aims to create sustainable solutions through her work. (event_time: 2023-02-04T09:48:00Z)\n  - Jolene had a successful outcome regarding her project. (event_time: 2023-06-26T09:17:00Z)\n  - Jolene is currently focusing on gaining more experience. (event_time: 2023-08-24T09:34:00Z)\n  - Jolene's recent accomplishment encourages her to keep striving in engineering (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:56:00Z)\n  - Jolene's recent accomplishment has stoked her love of engineering (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:56:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - robot: Jolene is working on a large, challenging, yet fun robotics project given by her engineering professor, which involves design and programming.\n  - problem-solving skills: Jolene is working on a huge, tough but fun robotics project from her engineering professor that is testing her creative and problem-solving skills.\n  - engineering professor: Jolene's engineering professor assigned a tough but fun robotics project requiring creativity and problem-solving.\n  - creative skills: Jolene's engineering professor assigned a huge robotics project that is challenging but fun, requiring creative and problem-solving skills.\n  - robotics project: Jolene's engineering professor assigned a huge robotics project. Jolene finds it tough but fun, enjoying the problem-solving and seeing the robot assemble.\n  - big project: Jolene has been working on a big project that is tough but cool to watch take shape, and she anticipates the final result.\n  - prototype: Jolene is working on a cool prototype that could revolutionize aerial surveillance.\n  - electrical engineering project: Jolene finished an electrical engineering project last week after a lot of work.\n  - milestone: Jolene finished a tough engineering project last month, calling it a big milestone she is proud of, having stuck it out despite problems. Deborah congratulated her.\n  - dreams: Jolene feels finishing a tough engineering project inspired her to keep striving for her dreams. Deborah recalls sharing dreams with her mom at a special place.\n  - Engineering assignments: Jolene is struggling to manage her Engineering assignments and is asking to discuss time management.\n  - the problems: Jolene gains a unique perspective on the problems by seeing art and design in various things. The problems were part of a tough engineering project Jolene finished last month, achieving a milestone.\n  - engineering project: Jolene wants her engineering projects to use her talents to solve important problems, inspired by her mom stressing helping others. She focuses on new ideas and efficiency.\n  - Research: Deborah states that research is key to success and encourages Jolene by mentioning that little steps and facing challenges make one stronger.\n  - work stress: Work stress is something that Jolene has been escaping for 3 years by playing a game.\n  - projects: Jolene is interested in projects that make a real difference, specifically sustainable initiatives and innovative environmental solutions, integrating values from loved ones.\n  - college: Jolene and her partner met in an engineering class in college, which later developed into a relationship.\n  - engineering class: Jolene and her partner met in an engineering class in college, which blossomed into their relationship.\n  - engineering student: Jolene, an engineering student, wants to use her talents to do good, solve important problems, be innovative, and improve efficiency, influenced by her mother's value of helping others.\n  - studying: Jolene has a schedule that includes studying, classes, and personal time, using yoga and meditation for balance.\n  - communities in need: Jolene wants to make a positive impact on communities in need by creating sustainable solutions through her engineering work.\n  - STEM: Jolene suggested a volunteer program where engineers teach STEM to underprivileged kids as a way to contribute.\n  - setback with Jolene's project: Jolene experienced a huge setback with her project last week, causing her to lose all her work, which was frustrating and depressing. Deborah offered support.\n  - studies: Jolene uses meditation to help her stay balanced during her studies.\n  - efforts: Deborah encouraged Jolene that her efforts will bear fruit and advised her not to give up.\n  - internship: Jolene is considering more internships to further enhance her skills after receiving positive feedback on her efforts, building on past experiences like a hectic internship.\n  - work files: Jolene lost her work files, which caused stress, but meditation helped her regain clarity.\n  - Green tech: Jolene wants to look into Green tech to see how she can contribute and suggested a volunteer program where engineers teach STEM to underprivileged kids.\n  - deadlines: Deborah expressed concern to Jolene about her exams and deadlines, noting the situation is difficult. Jolene confirmed it is tough, stressful, and requires her to constantly play catch-up.\n  - project: Deborah started a community cleanup project for fundraising. Jolene had a setback with her own project, losing all work, and Deborah supports her ambition.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1970,"context_chars":8246,"retrieval_duration":0.19313526153564453,"response_duration":3.374025821685791,"total_duration":3.5671610832214355,"grade":false,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer states that Jolene worked on the project for approximately 3 months and 5 days, which does not match the gold answer of 'four months'.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question about how long Jolene worked on the robotics project. It states that Jolene started working on the project on February 1, 2023, and finished it last month, which is May 2023. This indicates that she worked on the project for four months, aligning perfectly with the golden answer.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Jolene started working on the robotics project on February 1, 2023","Jolene finished the robotics project last month (May 2023)","The duration from February 1 to May 2023 is four months"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_3","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_3_qa_153","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What substitution does Nate suggest for butter in dairy-free baking?","golden_answer":"dairy-free margarine or coconut oil","hypothesis":"Nate suggests using dairy-free margarine or coconut oil as substitutes for butter in dairy-free baking.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time th